{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.1"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [1], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-001", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 1.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 1, "scanLeaf": 22}, "translationText": "Dhritarâshtra said :\nTell me, O Sanjaya! Assembled on Kurukshetra the centre of religious activity, desirous to fight, what indeed my people and the Pândavas did do?"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.2"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [2], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-002", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 2.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 2, "scanLeaf": 23}, "translationText": "Sanjaya said:\nBut then king Duryodhana, having seen the Pândava forces in battle-array, approached his teacher Drona, and spoke these words:"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.3"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [3], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-003", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 3.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 3, "scanLeaf": 24}, "translationText": "Behold, O Teacher ! this mighty army of the sons of Pându, arrayed by the son of Drupada, thy gifted pupil."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.4", "1.5", "1.6"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [4, 5, 6], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-004-006", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 4. 5. 6.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 4, "scanLeaf": 25}, "translationText": "Here (are) heroes, mighty archers, the equals in battle of Bhima and Arjuna—the great warriors Yuyudhâna, Virâta, Drupada ; the valiant Dhrishtaketu, Chekitâna and the king of Kâshi, the best of men Purujit, Kuntibhoja and Shaibya ; the powerful Yudhâmanyu and the brave Uttamaujas, the son of Subhadrâ, and the sons of Draupadi,—lords of great chariots."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.7"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [7], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-007", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 7.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 4, "scanLeaf": 25}, "translationText": "Hear also, O Best of the twice-born ! the names of those who (are) distinguished amongst ourselves, the leaders of my army. These I relate (to you) for your information."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.8"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [8], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-008", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 8.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 5, "scanLeaf": 26}, "translationText": "Thyself and Bhishma and Karna and Kripa, the victorious in war, Asvatthâma and Vikarna and Jayadratha, the son of Somadatta."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.9"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [9], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-009", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 9.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 5, "scanLeaf": 26}, "translationText": "And many other heroes also, well-skilled in fight, and armed with many kinds of weapons, are here determined to lay down their lives for my sake."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.10"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [10], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-010", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 10.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 6, "scanLeaf": 27}, "translationText": "This our army commanded by Bhishma (is) impossible to be counted, but that army of theirs, commanded by Bhima (is) easy to number."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.11"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [11], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-011", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 11.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 6, "scanLeaf": 27}, "translationText": "(Now) Do, being stationed in your proper places in the divisions of the army, support Bhishma alone."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.12"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [12], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-012", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 12.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 7, "scanLeaf": 28}, "translationText": "That powerful, eldest of the Kurus, Bhishma the grandsire, in order to cheer Duryodhana, now sounded aloud a lion-roar and blew his conch."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.13"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [13], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-013", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 13.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 7, "scanLeaf": 28}, "translationText": "Then following Bhishma, conches and kettle-drums, tabors, trumpets and cowhorns blared forth suddenly from the Kaurava side and the noise was tremendous."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.14"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [14], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-014", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 14.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 8, "scanLeaf": 29}, "translationText": "Then, also, Mâdhava and Pândava, stationed in their magnificent chariot yoked to white horses, blew their divine conches with a furious noise."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.15"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [15], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-015", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 15.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 8, "scanLeaf": 29}, "translationText": "Hrishikesha blew the Pânchajanya, Dhananjaya, the Devadatta, and Vrikodara, the doer of terrific deeds, his large conch Paundra."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.16"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [16], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-016", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 16.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 9, "scanLeaf": 30}, "translationText": "King Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, blew the conch named Anantavijaya, and Nakula and Sahadeva their Sughosha and Manipushpaka."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.17"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [17], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-017", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 17.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 9, "scanLeaf": 30}, "translationText": "The expert bowman, king of Kâshi, and the great warrior Shikhandi, Dhrishtadyumna and Virâta and the unconquered Sâtyaki;"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.18"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [18], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-018", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 18.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 10, "scanLeaf": 31}, "translationText": "O Lord of Earth ! Drupada and the sons of Draupadi, and the mighty-armed son of Subhadrâ, all also blew each his own conch."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.19"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [19], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-019", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 19.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 10, "scanLeaf": 31}, "translationText": "And the terrific noise resounding throughout heaven and earth rent the hearts of the Dhritarâshtra's party."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.20"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [20], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-020", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 20.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 11, "scanLeaf": 32}, "translationText": "Then, O Lord of Earth, seeing Dhritarâshtra army standing marshalled and the shooting about to begin, that Pândava whose ensign was the monkey, raising his bow, said the following words to Krishna :"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.21", "1.22"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [21, 22], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-021-022", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 21—22.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 11, "scanLeaf": 32}, "translationText": "Arjuna said :\nPlace my chariot, O Achyuta ! between the two armies that I may see those who stand here prepared for war. On this the eve of battle (let me know) with whom I have to fight."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.23"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [23], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-023", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 23.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 12, "scanLeaf": 33}, "translationText": "For I desire to observe those who are assembled here for fight, wishing to please the evil-minded Duryodhana by taking his part on this battle-field."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.24", "1.25"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [24, 25], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-024-025", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 24—25.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 13, "scanLeaf": 34}, "translationText": "Sanjaya said :\nCommanded thus by Gudâkesha, Hrishikesha, O Bhârata, drove that grandest of chariots to a place between the two hosts, facing Bhishma, Drona and all the rulers of the earth, and then spoke thus, “Behold, O Pârtha, all the Kurus gathered together!”"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.26"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [26], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: completion beyond page 13 not present in pinned scan; provisional secondary text."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-026", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 26.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 13, "scanLeaf": 34}, "translationText": "Then saw Pârtha stationed there in both the armies, grandfathers, fathers-in-law and uncles, brothers and cousins, his own and their sons and grandsons, and comrades, teachers, and other friends as well."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.27"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [27], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: printed pages 14–15 absent from pinned scan."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-027", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 27.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 14, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "Then he, the son of Kunti, seeing all those kinsmen stationed in their ranks, spoke thus sorrowfully, filled with deep compassion."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.28", "1.29"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [28, 29], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: pages missing; N→1 28—29 asserted by later Advaita OCR + Sacred Texts block structure, not by 1909 leaf image."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-028-029", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 28—29.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 15, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "Arjuna said :\nSeeing, O Krishna, these my kinsmen gathered here, eager for fight, my limbs fail me, and my mouth is parched up. I shiver all over, and my hair stands on end. The bow Gândiva slips from my hand, and my skin burns."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.30"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [30], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: printed pages 14–15 absent from pinned scan."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-030", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 30.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 15, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "Neither, O Keshava, can I stand upright. My mind is in a whirl. And I see adverse omens."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.31"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [31], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-031", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 31.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 16, "scanLeaf": 35}, "translationText": "Neither, Oh Krishna, do I see any good in killing these my own people in battle. I desire neither victory nor empire, nor yet pleasure."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.32", "1.33", "1.34"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [32, 33, 34], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: unit incomplete on pinned scan; tail from secondary PD transcription."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-032-034", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 32—34.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 16, "scanLeaf": 35}, "translationText": "Of what avail is dominion to us, of what avail are pleasures and even life, if these, O Govinda! for whose sake it is desired that empire, enjoyment and pleasure should be ours, themselves stand here in battle, having renounced life and wealth—\nTeachers, uncles, sons and also grandfathers, maternal uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, besides other kinsmen."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.35"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [35], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: printed pages 17–18 absent from pinned scan."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-035", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 35.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 17, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "Even though these were to kill me, O slayer of Madhu, I could not wish to kill them, not even for the sake of dominion over the three worlds, how much less for the sake of the earth!"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.36"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [36], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: printed pages 17–18 absent from pinned scan."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-036", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 36.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 18, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "What pleasure indeed could be ours, O Janârdana, from killing these sons of Dhritarâshtra? Sin only could take hold of us by the slaying of these felons."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.37"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [37], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: printed pages 17–18 absent from pinned scan."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-037", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 37.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 18, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "Therefore ought we not to kill our kindred, the sons of Dhritarâshtra. For how could we, O Mâdhava, gain happiness by the slaying of our own kinsmen?"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.38", "1.39"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [38, 39], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-038-039", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 38. 39.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 19, "scanLeaf": 36}, "translationText": "Though these, with understanding overpowered by greed, see no evil due to decay of families, and no sin in hostility to friends, why should we, O Janârdana, who see clearly the evil due to the decay of families, not turn away from this sin?"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.40"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [40], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-040", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 40.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 19, "scanLeaf": 36}, "translationText": "On the decay of a family the immemorial religious rites of that family die out. On the destruction of spirituality, impiety further overwhelms the whole of the family."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.41"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [41], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: printed pages 20–21 absent from pinned scan."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-041", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 41.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 20, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "On the prevalence of impiety, O Krishna, the women of the family become corrupt; and women being corrupted, there arises, O Vârshneya, intermingling of castes."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.42"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [42], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: printed pages 20–21 absent from pinned scan."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-042", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 42.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 20, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "Admixture of castes, indeed, is for the hell of the family and the destroyers of the family; their ancestors fall, deprived of the offerings of rice-ball and water."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.43"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [43], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: printed pages 20–21 absent from pinned scan."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-043", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 43.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 21, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "By these misdeeds of the destroyers of the family, bringing about confusion of castes, are the immemorial religious rites of the caste and the family destroyed."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.44"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [44], "editorialNotes": ["SOURCE_CONFLICT: printed pages 20–21 absent from pinned scan."], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "SOURCE_CONFLICT", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-044", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 44.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 21, "scanLeaf": 0}, "translationText": "We have heard, O Janârdana, that inevitable is the dwelling in hell of those men in whose families religious practices have been destroyed."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.45"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [45], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-045", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 45.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 22, "scanLeaf": 37}, "translationText": "Alas, we are involved in a great sin, in that we are prepared to slay our kinsmen, from greed of the pleasures of a kingdom!"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.46"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [46], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-046", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 46.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 22, "scanLeaf": 37}, "translationText": "Verily, if the sons of Dhritarâshtra, weapons in hand, were to slay me, unresisting and unarmed, in the battle, that would be better for me."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.47"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [47], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Swami Swarupananda", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "segmentId": "swarupananda-1909-bg-1-047", "sourceChecksum": "ab9e38c2f252574de88d55374fb8c97c7c2998b4442e9e8f32cda8713a99315e", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-swarupananda-1909-v1", "sourceLabel": "I. 47.", "sourcePage": {"printed": 23, "scanLeaf": 38}, "translationText": "Sanjaya said :\nSpeaking thus in the midst of the battle-field, Arjuna casting away his bow and arrows, sank down on the seat of his chariot, with his mind distressed with sorrow."}
